What is an API?

A REST API exposes resources (payments, orders, users, etc.) via HTTP methods like GET, POST, PUT, DELETE using JSON payloads and status codes.
​

In payments, APIs cover create payment, authorize, capture, refund, list transactions, etc., with strict contracts and idempotency requirements.

What is API test automation?

Programmatically sending HTTP requests to the API and asserting on:

Status codes (200, 201, 400, 401, 422, 500, etc.).

Response body (fields, types, values, schema).

Headers, cookies, auth behavior.

Non‑functional aspects (latency, rate limits, etc.).
​

Tests run automatically in pipelines and can gate deployments.
